    "title": "Southeast Texas voters to decide on Emergency Service District sales tax proposals this November - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Jefferson County, Texas\nSoutheast Texas voters to decide on Emergency Service District sales tax proposals this November\n8 hours ago\nBEAUMONT, Texas — Voters in Jefferson, Orange, Hardin, and Tyler counties will soon decide whether to dedicate a portion of the state’s existing 8.25% sales tax to local Emergency Services Districts (ESDs) to strengthen fire protection and emergency medical response. Officials stress this is not a tax increase...\n1",
